# 21 CFR Part 11 client walkthrough (smalt emulator)

Browser console walkthrough of the Part 11 faces on the smalt substrate. All
networking through `smaltFetch` (`workspace/lib/smalt.ts`, loopback-only).

## 0. Quiescent substrate

```bash
just substrate-up   # scripts/substrate.sh, lock fd closed
eval "$(just relay-env)"
```

## 1. Blob WORM record commit (immutability policy = Part 11 retention)

Each record below commits into a Blob container locked by an immutability
policy (routes: `lib/smalt/egress_router.ex:1313/1563/2282`; WORM face
`lib/smalt/data_plane/blob_storage.ex:273`).

{% for row in worm_stores %}
- Container `{{ row.container }}`, policy `{{ row.policy }}`.
{% endfor %}

```js
// commit + lock, per record
{% for row in records %}
await smaltFetch(`/blob/{{ row.container }}/{{ row.record }}`, {
  method: "PUT",
  headers: { "x-ms-immutability-policy-until-date": "{{ row.policy }}" },
  body: JSON.stringify({ id: "{{ row.record }}", label: "{{ row.label }}" }),
});
{% endfor %}
```

## 2. Attestation face for the signing host

`POST /attest/:type` (`lib/smalt/egress/AttestRoutes.ex:17` →
`lib/smalt/security/attestation.ex:1`) proves the signing workstation is
enclave-backed before its e-signature is accepted (21 CFR 11.10(k)).

```js
{% for row in hosts %}
await smaltFetch("{{ row.route }}", {
  method: "POST",
  body: JSON.stringify({ host: "{{ row.host }}", fingerprint: "{{ row.fingerprint }}" }),
});
{% endfor %}
```

## 3. AppConfig quality-policy gate

The quality validation step evaluates the Part 11 enforcement flag before
disposition (`lib/smalt/egress/AppConfigRoutes.ex:50`;
`appconfig_features.ex:100 evaluate/3`).

```js
{% for row in flags %}
const part11 = await smaltFetch("/kv/appconfig/evaluate", {
  method: "POST",
  body: JSON.stringify({ feature: "{{ row.key }}", context: { record: "batch-101" } }),
});
if (!part11.enabled) throw new Error("Part 11 policy gate closed");
{% endfor %}
```

## 4. KV PS256 e-signature

E-signatures sign with KV PS256 (`lib/smalt/data_plane/kv_pss.ex:1-8`,
externally verifiable; KD-105/KD-119) and bind to the signing agent — gate
010 of this pack refuses any record whose signature does not bind a
`prov:Agent`.

## 5. Gates

The pack's four refusal gates run over the consumer graph (`qualification/verify.py`):
signature-missing (010), audit-trail-missing (020), capa-missing (030),
mutation-non-WORM (040). A mutation attempted outside the WORM path is a typed
refusal, not a silent write.